WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.030 --> 00:00:04.589
Everything starts the day your mum's egg
meets your dad's sperm.

00:00:04.589 --> 00:00:10.110
Four weeks later your little brain
begins to form. Epidemiologist David

00:00:10.110 --> 00:00:14.299
Barker says, that whilst developing
inside our mother, we are receiving

00:00:14.299 --> 00:00:19.619
postcards from the outside world. These
postcards tell us if this world is

00:00:19.619 --> 00:00:25.740
dangerous or safe, if food is plentiful or scarce. Knowing nothing else, we learn

00:00:25.740 --> 00:00:31.650
from those messages. Let's watch what we
experience and learn inside the womb

00:00:31.650 --> 00:00:42.059
from the fetus perspective. Month 1: only
24 hours alive every bit of genetic

00:00:42.059 --> 00:00:47.100
information is already present in a
single cell: from our hair color to our

00:00:47.100 --> 00:00:52.680
talent as a future pianist. Then we
divide ourselves again and again. After

00:00:52.680 --> 00:00:58.320
around a week we travel from the ovaries
to the uterus where we then undergo the

00:00:58.320 --> 00:01:03.840
great divide - splitting into two, half of
which will become us while the other

00:01:03.840 --> 00:01:09.090
half forms the placenta which brings us
food and oxygen and carries away waste.

00:01:09.090 --> 00:01:14.430
By week four we have developed into a
small being that is growing at a rate of

00:01:14.430 --> 00:01:20.580
1 million cells per second. Our spinal
cord, heart and brain are now clearly

00:01:20.580 --> 00:01:28.710
visible, even if we adjust the size of a
poppyseed. Month 2: at about week four to

00:01:28.710 --> 00:01:33.930
five our heart starts to beat and we are
now ten thousand times bigger than we

00:01:33.930 --> 00:01:38.939
were at conception. This is a crucial
point in our neurological development as

00:01:38.939 --> 00:01:44.220
our brain grows at a rate of around a
hundred thousand cells each minute. If

00:01:44.220 --> 00:01:50.280
our mother consumes alcohol and drugs or
experiences extreme stress or trauma our

00:01:50.280 --> 00:01:55.229
tiny brain can get damaged. This can lead
to maths problems at school or even

00:01:55.229 --> 00:02:01.920
schizophrenia some forty years later. If
our mum stays healthy and can relax our

00:02:01.920 --> 00:02:08.509
brain can develop to its full potential.
We are now the size of a raspberry.

00:02:09.170 --> 00:02:15.569
Month 3: at the beginning of month
three we start to react to stimuli. Our

00:02:15.569 --> 00:02:20.010
sense of smell is developing and
exposure to toxins can make us cringe.

00:02:20.010 --> 00:02:26.280
Our brain is continuing to grow very
fast our Ears start forming and we can

00:02:26.280 --> 00:02:32.250
soon hear our mum's heartbeat and voice
speak. Still small enough we have plenty

00:02:32.250 --> 00:02:36.989
of space to move inside the belly. Our
mother's womb becomes our sensory

00:02:36.989 --> 00:02:43.739
playground we learn to move our arms,
stretch our fingers, smile or suck our

00:02:43.739 --> 00:02:49.799
thumb. 75% of us are now showing a
preference to use the right hand we are

00:02:49.799 --> 00:02:58.769
now around the size of a lemon. Month 4:
our head makes up about half our total

00:02:58.769 --> 00:03:05.310
size. We learn to kick, pee and how to
swallow. Our taste buds are developing. If

00:03:05.310 --> 00:03:10.349
our mother eats a wide variety of things
we learn to appreciate different tastes

00:03:10.349 --> 00:03:15.450
and become less fussy eaters later in
life. If we receive inadequate or poor

00:03:15.450 --> 00:03:21.000
nutrients we adapt our physiology to
sustain our development. This process is

00:03:21.000 --> 00:03:25.410
also called fetal programming. Some
researchers have found that this can

00:03:25.410 --> 00:03:30.480
result in health problems such as
obesity, heart conditions and diabetes

00:03:30.480 --> 00:03:39.810
later in life. We are now around the size
of a big tomato. Month 5: while earlier

00:03:39.810 --> 00:03:45.090
our mums voice sounded muffled now it is
starting to become clear. We are also

00:03:45.090 --> 00:03:49.829
experiencing a big growth spurt and we
start the development of our teeth and

00:03:49.829 --> 00:03:55.950
our first real hair, fingernails, eyebrows
and eyelashes. We are becoming more

00:03:55.950 --> 00:04:02.430
active each day and enjoying flexing our
tiny muscles. As we wriggle, kick and turn

00:04:02.430 --> 00:04:07.290
our mother will start to feel as moving.
If she responds we learned that for

00:04:07.290 --> 00:04:14.420
every action there is a reaction. We are
now around the size of a dragon fruit.

00:04:17.910 --> 00:04:24.009
During this sixth month a major mark of
brain development occurs. Our brains

00:04:24.009 --> 00:04:29.199
cerebral cortex splits into two
hemispheres. But it's also an exciting

00:04:29.199 --> 00:04:34.630
month for our eyes which open for the
first time. Even though we see only blurs

00:04:34.630 --> 00:04:40.060
we start to respond to light. Some say
it's good if our mum now takes us into

00:04:40.060 --> 00:04:45.370
the sun. We are now starting to make
simple facial expressions such as

00:04:45.370 --> 00:04:50.229
forming a grin. We probably learn to
communicate for the time when we are

00:04:50.229 --> 00:04:55.120
born when we want to show our feelings.
We are now around the size of a small

00:04:55.120 --> 00:05:04.539
cauliflower. Month 7: we begin to develop
regular intervals for sleeping and being

00:05:04.539 --> 00:05:09.610
awake. The hair on our head is now
clearly visible and our milk teeth have

00:05:09.610 --> 00:05:15.130
formed under our gums. When we hear our
mum speak we may respond with an

00:05:15.130 --> 00:05:20.080
increased heartbeat and movement. Some
researchers claim that we now begin to

00:05:20.080 --> 00:05:25.419
learn language from hearing the voices
from outside because once born we seem

00:05:25.419 --> 00:05:30.220
to show a preference for our dads and
mums native language. If we were to be

00:05:30.220 --> 00:05:35.199
born now we would have a 90% chance of
survival and arrived the size of a

00:05:35.199 --> 00:05:43.330
pineapple. Month 8 we are now behaving
like a newborn. Our brain is functional

00:05:43.330 --> 00:05:48.009
and our nervous system ready. Our lungs
are almost fully formed and we are

00:05:48.009 --> 00:05:53.620
practicing breathing by inhaling and the
amniotic fluid. Ee now spend almost all of

00:05:53.620 --> 00:05:59.080
our time as sleep, maybe dreaming about
our near future. In preparation for birth

00:05:59.080 --> 00:06:04.389
most of us will have now turned upside
down. To get through that tiny hole at

00:06:04.389 --> 00:06:09.550
the end of the tunnel our bones and
skull are still extremely flexible. Only

00:06:09.550 --> 00:06:12.220
the immune system is still in its
infancy.

00:06:12.220 --> 00:06:16.840
It will take many months after birth
until our internal body guards can fully

00:06:16.840 --> 00:06:23.319
protect our health. We are now around the
size of a melon.

00:06:23.319 --> 00:06:30.740
Month 9:  in the last month we keep
practicing our motor skills and kicks.

00:06:30.740 --> 00:06:36.949
When our mum laughs eat sweets or drinks
an ice tea we might respond by bouncing

00:06:36.949 --> 00:06:41.629
up and down. If we could already
understand research papers we would now

00:06:41.629 --> 00:06:45.770
hope that our mum can bring us to the
world through natural birth which

00:06:45.770 --> 00:06:50.569
protects us through a stronger immune
system for life. The puzzle of what is

00:06:50.569 --> 00:06:55.819
nurture and what is nature is now well
underway and already shows a first image

00:06:55.819 --> 00:07:00.740
of our character. The most important
missing piece will be added in our early

00:07:00.740 --> 00:07:08.169
childhood. At the end of the nine months
we are around the size of a jackfruit.

00:07:08.169 --> 00:07:13.999
After many hours of hard labour
we will be welcomed into this world. Some

00:07:13.999 --> 00:07:18.349
will then be instantly taken away for
various checkup procedures and bathing.

00:07:18.349 --> 00:07:24.349
But if we are lucky we will first spend
some time with our mum. If placed on her

00:07:24.349 --> 00:07:26.719
belly
we will instinctively crawl to her

00:07:26.719 --> 00:07:32.659
breast and then show us sucking skills.
This makes us happy, full and feel safe.

00:07:32.659 --> 00:07:37.509
The foundation for all future learning

00:07:45.139 --> 00:07:47.199
 

